    "method": "model"
   },
   {
    "act": "claude-13-turn-298-f-s5-0",
    "kind": "explain",
    "text": "Of course, we have nearly 40 years or improvements in what \"graphics\" means so we can make graphics that are clickable \u2026",
    "verdict": "noted",
    "by": "claude-13-turn-298-r-3",
    "mark": "\u329f",
    "quote": "Your Emacs works in a terminal, so it can't show the SVG.",
    "method": "model"
   },
   {
    "act": "claude-13-turn-298-f-s6-0",
    "kind": "propose",
    "text": "Anyway, I think we need to work out a graphical representation for a cascade.",
    "verdict": "deferred",
    "by": "claude-13-turn-298-r-4",
    "mark": "\ud83c\ude38",
    "quote": "Shall I send the renderer job now, in parallel, working from the 10-24 lab's real squares?",
    "method": "model"
   },
   {
    "act": "claude-13-turn-298-f-s7-0",
    "kind": "extend",
    "text": "./futon5a/essays/moran-1971-agent-cascades/reading-moran-1971.md is worth rereading and figure-1-cascade-of-64-patterns\u2026",
    "verdict": "not-answered",
    "by": null,
    "mark": null,
    "quote": "",
    "method": "model"
   },
   {
    "act": "claude-13-turn-298-f-s8-0",
    "kind": "qualify",
    "text": "Of course, underneath that we'll have our category theory model.",
    "verdict": "not-answered",
    "by": null,
    "mark": null,
    "quote": "",
    "method": "model"
   },
   {
    "act": "claude-13-turn-298-f-s9-0",
    "kind": "constrain",
    "text": "But, basicaly, the acceptance condition for this criterion is to develop a *graphical* stepper.",
    "verdict": "noted",
    "by": "claude-13-turn-298-r-3",
    "mark": "\u329f",
    "quote": "The text stepper keeps its job, and the pictures go to Mojira and the web page.",
    "method": "model"
   },
   {
    "act": "claude-13-turn-298-f-s10-0",
    "kind": "explain",
    "text": "On the one hand, each turn can be thought of as \"potentially\" a cascade (a null cascade if no patterns are found) and s\u2026",
    "verdict": "noted",
    "by": "claude-13-turn-298-r-0",
    "mark": "\ud83c\ude16",
    "quote": "A turn with no occurrence has a null cascade, as you said.",
    "method": "model"
   },
   {
    "act": "claude-13-turn-298-f-s10-1",
    "kind": "propose",
    "text": "which could run vertically, a bit like the famous git merge diagrams,",
    "verdict": "not-answered",
    "by": null,
    "mark": null,
    "quote": "",
    "method": "model"
   },
   {
    "act": "claude-13-turn-298-f-s11-0",
    "kind": "report-problem",
    "text": "We had some start on something like this in the Voxterm \"Diagram\" tab but it wasn't complete yet.",
    "verdict": "not-answered",
    "by": null,
    "mark": null,
    "quote": "",
    "method": "model"
   },
   {
    "act": "claude-13-turn-298-f-s12-0",
    "kind": "explain",
    "text": "The relevance to the GCC is is that the local cascades would all be local regions inside the GCC.",
    "verdict": "not-answered",
    "by": null,
    "mark": null,
    "quote": "",
    "method": "model"
   }
